<title>UK: Thorn up on NatWest buy note.</title>
<headline>Thorn up on NatWest buy note.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in electronic rentals group Thorn Plc gained over three percent on Wednesday, helped by a buy note from NatWest Securities, market sources said.</p>
<p>Thorn shares rose as high as 377p but slipped slightly to trade at 375p by 1141 GMT, up 11p or three percent on the day. The broader market was down 0.22 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;The share has been weak of late so it was due a rebound and the NatWest buy note lent support,&quot; a marketmaker said.</p>
<p>Analysts at NatWest were unavailable for comment.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
